      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "CLDN16 has no extracellular terminus (N- and C-termini are both intracellular); the only extracellular regions are ECL1 (residues 27\u201379) and ECL2 (residues 141\u2013163). The HA tag overlaps with the anti-loop antibody signal on the cell surface, and in claudin biology 'the loop' antibody targets ECL1 (the larger, 53-residue loop). No residue is named in any of L1\u2013L3, so the junction cannot be pinned; the site is reported at region level. ECL1 spans 53 residues with a safe interior zone (\u22653 from TM boundaries) of residues 30\u201376. Full-length HA-tagged CLDN16 expressed in MDCK and HeLa cells; the HA signal co-localised with an anti-loop antibody (raised against the extracellular loop of Cldn16) on the cell surface by immunofluorescence, confirming the HA tag is displayed on the extracellular face within the loop region.",
